Reading: gamma_c(R) is the NECESSARY-condition floor at finite R.  Any
construction rate must be >= it.  If the empirical construction threshold
gamma_R equals gamma_c(R), the construction is TIGHT against the necessary
condition; if gamma_R is stuck at 3/5 while gamma_c(R) is well below, the
gap is a CONSTRUCTION deficiency, not a capacity one.
Demonstrating the trap on the cases just found:
  R= 32 gamma=1/2=0.5000 D0=3:  EFFECTIVE rate = 0.593750   (gamma_c(32) = 0.500000)
  R= 32 gamma=49/100=0.4900 D0=4:  EFFECTIVE rate = 0.606061   (gamma_c(32) = 0.500000)
  R= 32 gamma=48/100=0.4800 D0=4:  EFFECTIVE rate = 0.593750   (gamma_c(32) = 0.500000)
  R= 64 gamma=3/5=0.6000 D0=0:  EFFECTIVE rate = 0.600000   (gamma_c(64) = 0.543478)
  R= 32 gamma=3/5=0.6000 D0=0:  EFFECTIVE rate = 0.600000   (gamma_c(32) = 0.500000)

